<p><strong>PROBLEM 15</strong>-45 Show the relative energy levels of the seven <i>&pi;</i> molecular orbitals of the cycloheptatrienyl system. Tell which of the seven orbitals are filled in the cation, radical, and anion, and account for the aromaticity of the cycloheptatrienyl cation.</p>

<p><strong>PROBLEM 15</strong>-46 1-Phenyl-2-butene has an ultraviolet absorption at <i>&lambda;</i><sub>max</sub> = 208 nm (<i>&epsilon;</i> = 8000). On treatment with a small amount of strong acid, isomerization occurs and a new substance with <i>&lambda;</i><sub>max</sub> = 250 nm (<i>&epsilon;</i> = 15,800) is formed. Propose a structure for this isomer, and suggest a mechanism for its formation.</p>

